{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ModelsOfQous.PhysicalUnitsGapLinear","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ModelsOfQous.PhysicalUnitsGapLinear","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.gap_bound_vanishes_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.gap_bound_vanishes_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/physical-units-gap-linear.lean#L26-L31","doc":"At the symmetric point the categorical bound vanishes identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.physical_units_gap_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.physical_units_gap_linear","kind":"theorem","line":11,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/physical-units-gap-linear.lean#L11-L24","doc":"**Physically normalised gap vanishes linearly.**  With\n`ℏ_q = (q−1)/q`, the crossing-energy gap bound\n`Δ_q = E_×(q)·(q−1)²` satisfies the exact identity\n`Δ_q / ℏ_q² = q(q−1)(q+1)/2`: the archimedean normalisation buys\nback two of the three vanishing orders at `q = 1`, no more. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:physical-units-gap-linear","label":"prop:physical-units-gap-linear","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/physical-units-gap-linear.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.crossingEnergyGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.crossingEnergyGap","kind":"def","line":6,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/physical-units-gap-linear.lean#L6-L9","doc":"Crossing energy `E_×(q) = (q − q⁻¹)/2`, local form for this\nstatement; to be unified with the climax-volume-mass declaration when\nthe proof is discharged. ","signatureChunk":0}]}